		(uuid "88189d6b-0e32-5557-8869-d0882feff8ad")
	)
	(text_box "H-bridge drive (BIOZ_DRV_MODE = 2): EL1 and EL4 switch between AVDD and AGND; current = AVDD / (2 x Rseries) = 1.8 / (2 x 30 k) = 30 uA (square), set by the resistors, not by the chip [CALC]. The chip does not limit current in this mode:\nthe 2.35 nF per pad blocks DC (single-fault: one capacitor shorted still blocks). 20 k is DPCR's lowest standard value (5 kV pulse-tested); 10 k inner limits the pin current to <= 0.7 mA (MAX30009 abs max +/-50 mA, pins clamp to AGND per\nits Figure 12).\nExternal 5 kV pulse: <= 5 kV / 20 k = 0.25 A edge current, tau = 20 k x 2.35 nF = 47 us, ~29 mJ into the resistor [CALC]. DRVSJ, DRVXC, DRVXR unconnected (ADI defibrillation application circuit, H-bridge mode).\nIdle: MUX_EN = 0 (reset default) disconnects all EL pins (datasheet register text) — required by contract §10 ('idle drive outputs high-impedance'); the unpowered pin state is NOT stated by the datasheet [UNVERIFIED]."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 268.335 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fa24e223-8196-5547-a3a1-940794fefc85")
	)
	(text_box "Sense taps (EL2B = BIP from pad A, EL3B = BIN from pad B): DPCR2512 51 k + TVS to GND + 20 k"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 314.055 25.4 0)
		(size 190.35 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fa885358-b126-5021-8cc2-b778af03c6a3")
	)
	(text_box "EL2B/EL3B use the chip's internal high-pass (no external capacitor), so the patient's DC potential (set by the main front end's RLD bias, ~1.65 V) is blocked inside the\nchip; DC current through these pins <= ~15 nA [CALC from the 48 Mohm input impedance]. 20 k inner resistors as in ADI's defibrillation application (RSEC 20 k). Pin\ncurrent under the 5 kV test <= (7 V)/20 k = 0.35 mA.\nEL2A/EL3A (external-coupling variants) unconnected. No test points (R9)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 314.055 31.75 0)
		(size 190.35 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3a9da113-dce7-5d0d-8212-16db22894f6e")
	)
	(text_box "U1601 MAX30009 (WLP-25), 4-wire calibration resistor, VREF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 314.055 86.216 0)
		(size 233.145 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9bb6fbd1-5850-5603-bbe5-fdcfd639fa1b")
	)
	(text_box "Supplies AVDD = DVDD = 1V8_SUP (1.7-2.0 V), each 0.1 uF + 10 uF (pin table). VREF 1 uF. Operating range -40 to +85 C (datasheet, four places) - the design's [UNVERIFIED] item is now answered; the device\nitself is the narrowest-range part on these sheets.\nCalibration: R1609 100 ohm 0.05 % across the CAL port (CAL1+CAL2 to one end, CAL3+CAL4 to the other, Kelvin at the resistor) for the datasheet's per-frequency gain/phase calibration; absolute accuracy of\nthe pad reading also depends on the 5 % DPCR drive resistors (current is set by them in H-bridge mode) -> factory calibration at the pad connector with the other chip in its specified state (F-9) [whether\nthe CAL port calibration applies in H-bridge mode is UNVERIFIED].\nCarrier: 96 kHz proposed (PLL 24.576 MHz = 750 x 32.768 kHz, KDIV 1, DAC_OSR 256) instead of 128 kHz (contract issue 1). FCLK unconnected (datasheet: allowed), TRIG to GND (datasheet: when unused).\nInterface: CSB/I2C_SEL = SBZ_CS_N with the contract's 100 k pull-up (SPI mode; firmware sets DISABLE_I2C). SCLK, SDI tolerate 5.5 V, so 3.3 V inputs are fine. SDO is a 1.8 V output (abs max 2.2 V): U1603\nSN74LVC1T45 (A on 1V8_SUP, B on 3V3_SUP, DIR = A->B, Ioff both ports) drives SBZ_MISO at 3.3 V levels; R1612 holds A low while SDO is tri-stated. INT open drain, pulled up on 05."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 314.055 92.566 0)
		(size 233.145 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2accc159-03e3-5d6a-9cb5-bcd0cebe7905")
	)
	(text_box "1V8_SUP: TPS7A2018 from 3V3_SUP (made here, contract §4) + 1 k bleed as the rail's sink for injected current"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 114.425 0)
		(size 186.44 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c464fb91-8129-583a-ba37-4ba765adb64b")
	)
	(text_box "TPS7A2018PDBVR: 1.6-6.0 V in, 300 mA, 7 uVrms, -40..+125 C TJ; EN tied to IN (rail follows 3V3_SUP). COUT total ~22 uF (0.47-200 uF allowed).\nNo TVS exists that clamps below the MAX30009's 2.2 V abs max (lowest VBR found 4.0 V), so the contract's rail shunt clamp is replaced by a guaranteed sink: R1610 1\nk = 1.8 mA, larger than the worst current the inner resistors can inject into the rail (<= ~1.1 mA) [CALC; notes]. Cost 3.2 mW while the supervisor rail is on."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 120.775 0)
		(size 186.44 8.477)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "30de7e6d-a05c-51cf-b893-58a3bfe8a852")
	)
